# temple-run 1.43.0 (Google Play, Unity il2cpp, arm64 only -> native bridge). Positions read at 562x900 content.
# Fresh root: intro flight -> "Thanks! ... 500 Coins" popup over the menu (every fresh root) -> two event popups + a challenge-screen visit while a Global Challenge runs -> menu with idol + PLAY -> run; the tutorial does not wait for a swipe (the runner dies at the first corner and the run restarts by itself).
size 562 900
needs arm64
control break-input
unreachable first corner passed: the turn window is a fraction of a second of a moving picture; S1 + S4 probes passed it in some runs only, and no log line or still picture marks the window
unreachable save-me ad: AppLovin content from the network
unreachable ad end: AppLovin content from the network
unreachable score: drawn digits only, no log line
# menu scene loaded (Unity log); the intro flight follows, then the popup
wait-log app "WARMING DONE" 180000
wait-log app "[TemplePrefab] System RAM" 60000
# the menu animates (idol glow): stability is judged on the popup's rectangle, after the close on its title band (above the idol)
wait-changed 40 300 480 280 20000
wait-stable 40 300 480 280 20000 1500
mark popup 40 300 480 100
# the panel's plain left border: pixel-equal in the coins and "Global Challenges" popups, the menu's wall when no popup is up
mark panel 48 450 24 50
expect-varied 40 300 480 280
touch 280 540 150
# the popup closes within the touch (the next one, if any, is up at once): compare against the mark, not against a wait's own start
wait-stable 40 300 480 100 10000 1000
expect-changed popup 40 300 480 100
# while a server-driven Global Challenge runs (seen 2026-11-19, 4d 9h left on the menu's event icon) two more popups follow, none logged,
# and PLAY stays inert until the challenge screen has been opened once (an arrow points at its icon): close both, open it, BACK
if-same panel
touch 280 540 150
# "Cumulative Distance" popup: its title sits in this band, its Close at PLAY's spot
wait-stable 40 200 480 100 10000 1000
touch 280 625 150
wait-stable 40 200 480 100 10000 1000
touch 480 405 150
wait-stable 40 40 480 100 10000 1000
touch 280 845 150
wait-stable 40 200 480 100 10000 1000
end
mark menu
touch 280 625 150
# GameController reloads the upgrade levels when a run starts (absent after WARMING DONE without PLAY, S1 r0)
wait-log app "[CRASH GetPlayerLevelForUpgradeType" 20000
wait 2500
expect-changed menu
# one swipe at a fixed delay from the marker went unlogged in some runs (+2.5 s 5/5, +5.5 s 1/2 gate passes: the runner is dead by then), and back-to-back swipes register none (S4 s4-tr-b3)
# so swipes repeat over ~+2.5..+6 s, a few frames apart; wait-frames is no checkpoint, so the wait-log below sees every one
# left swipes: the first corner turns right, so none turns and DirectSwipeDetector logs them (a right swipe inside the corner window turns and logs nothing: gate s4-gate1)
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-frames 3
touch-swipe 480 600 200 600 120
wait-log app "LEFT: turn element was null" 5000
# floor = half the lowest of 3 means over this window, WSL x86_64 readback, job s4-tr-b4: 25.7 / 26.2 / 33.3
expect-fps 12.8 tier=readback over 4000
expect-audio 5000
expect-no-log services "refused IActivityTaskManager"
